<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore share index falls on budget, currencies.</title>
<headline>Singapore share index falls on budget, currencies.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's key Straits Times Industrials (STI) index hit a low of 1,958.30 on Monday afternoon following a disappointing budget and concerns over regional currencies, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0713 GMT, the index was down nine points at 1,958.14, a shade off its 30-month low of 1,956.21.</p>
